# Nihonium · Nh · gate 113

**Nihonium** (Nh) is element **113** of the periodic table — a **post-transition metal**, period 7, group 13, p-block, solid (predicted) at standard conditions, atomic weight **[286] (most stable isotope)**.

## The element (carbon layer — reference chemistry)
The first element named in Japan ('Nihon'); a flicker of a second of existence.

## The gate (silicon layer — the 118 Gates)
Under David Wise's four-state cycle, gate **113** falls on **0:1 — first valley** because (Z−1) mod 4 = **0**. That state is *the first reach of emptiness toward one — potential, charge, the rising edge* — the nature of emergence here is **electrical**. Nihonium is not a thing apart; it is the one stochastic element, caught at this beat of its cycle.

## Emergence — electrical
This emergent carries the **electrical** nature: the same four — natural · ethereal · spiritual · electrical — that run through every sphere of UD0. Its color is `#3fd0e0`.

